  "limits": [
    "The same upstream083861/llamabd4f bases, valid-Mel frames, owned pool, model bytes, portable armv8.2-a+dotprod+fp16 target and geometry remain. Only CPU Diarizer backend_params caps the existing default request to min(requested, hardware_concurrency); unknown0 falls back1. GPU requests keep their existing settings. New exact profile identity gen2-valid-mel-pool-cpu-v2; no Rust loader admission yet.",
    "Source/nativeGGML composition, actual compiler inputs and package payload closure must be audited. All build/test/control children deny weight-format reads and network access. Construction has no model acquisition.",
    "Public C ABI control performs101failed model-construction attempts with a nonexistent readonly path. This exercises backend setup and destructor/exception cleanup; it is not successful model loading, frontend execution or neural inference.",
    "Retain all101 immediate and settled thread counts, each10\u2013100ms wait and any failure evidence under the existing warmup+2 incidental-thread allowance. This verifies missing-model cleanup rather than successful load or live resource use. Compile-time policy checks cover0/1/2/3/4/14 reported CPUs and a smaller requested cap.",
    "Require the exact new version at the public C ABI, native diar_state CTest and strict private package loader audit. Deliver the failed-load helper binary in a safe filesystem archive so its payload can be independently rehashed.",
    "Bind current local imports before importing and verify committed source/protocol before preparation. Successful construction alone does not qualify Rust/public numerical parity, lifecycle, long-session, mixed-model, quality, platform, app, signing or release gates. No neural calls or asset acquisition in this construction; later qualifications must explicitly bind this new identity."
  ]
